For EVERY PMID, list the study's OWN results (from the results part of the abstract, not from the background or the authors' general conclusions). One entry per measured outcome:
- outcome: what was measured, in the abstract's words;
- groups: what was compared (e.g. "intervention vs control", "before vs after in one group", "pooled RCTs");
- comparison: between_groups | within_group | pooled | none;
- direction: increase | decrease | no_difference | mixed | not_stated;
- significant: true | false | null (null when no test or interval is given);
- quote: the sentence of the abstract, copied exactly, that gives this result.
A paper with no own result (a narrative review, a protocol, a methods paper) gets "results": [].

Reply with a single JSON object and nothing else:
